  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 4602.06 Transfer of Certificates or Permits",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-06-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 4602.06 Transfer of Certificates or Permits.\n\n(a) A carrier wishing to transfer its certificate or permit shall notify the bureau in writing of the proposed transaction and the name of the prospective transferee.\n\n(b) Within 30 days of receipt of the written notice, as specified in (a) above, the bureau shall request a transfer application Form DSAD 5-HT, “Transfer of Household Goods Carrier Operations”, (rev. 12/23), from the prospective transferee in order to evaluate the proposed transfer.\n\n(c) The scope of the evaluation shall be limited to the following issues:\n\n(1) Whether the transferee is willing and able; and\n\n(2) Whether the transferee has complied with relevant statutes and these rules.\n\nSource. #5852, eff 6-23-94; ss by #7240, eff 6-23-00, EXPIRED: 6-23-08\n\nNew. #9379, eff 1-30-09; ss by #12358, eff 8-2-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c4600.html"
